		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>I have a postgreSql data base.</p><p>In this database i have two tables with the same Foreignkey (who is User)</p><p>so i have a table A (list of all user) and a table B (list of user i follow)</p><p>and i would like to filter the table A and also add a new colomn who tell me if the user is in the table B or not.</p><p>For the moment i do this in multiple task :</p><p>&#160; &#160; first i get the filter list of user in the table A<br />&#160; &#160; second i get the filter list of user in the table B<br />&#160; &#160; third i parse the table A and for each user i check if it is present or not in the table B</p><p>My question is : can i do this more efficiently ?? in one query for exemple ?</p><p>I hope i am clear enough</p><p>thank you in advance for your answer</p><p>I try to optimise my code If someone have an idea I&#039;m all ears</p>]]></content>
